{"hash":"eca76f659a419a41","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":89.556,"said":"Here in the court, hear Srisailam’s best-loved legend, from the Shiva Purana. Shiva and Parvati had two sons, Ganesha and Kartikeya. When the time came for them to marry, the parents set a contest: whoever went around the whole earth first would be married first. Kartikeya set off at once. Ganesha stayed. He walked seven times around his mother and father and bowed to them, for to him they were the whole world. So Ganesha was married first. When Kartikeya returned, the sage Narada told him what had happened. He was deeply hurt. He left home and went away to the Krauncha mountain to live alone. Parvati grieved. Shiva sent sages to bring their son back, but he would not come. So the parents went themselves, and still he moved further away. What can parents do when a child will not come home? They stay close. The Purana says Shiva visits him on the new-moon day, and Parvati on the full moon. The linga that arose here became famous in all three worlds as Mallikarjuna; many explain the name as Mallika for Parvati and Arjuna for Shiva. And the Mother has her own shrine here. Let us go to the western terrace to meet her.\n\nDid you know? The Shiva Purana adds that Ganesha’s two sons were Kshema and Labha, ‘well-being’ and ‘gain’.","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":1131},{"key":"didYouKnow","start":1147,"end":1240}],"words":[[0.098,0.373,0,4],[0.483,0.084,5,7],[0.579,0.072,8,11],[0.663,0.421,12,17],[1.288,0.264,19,23],[1.564,0.721,24,35],[2.298,0.625,36,46],[2.935,0.493,47,53],[3.68,0.228,55,59],[3.92,0.084,60,63],[4.016,0.349,64,69],[4.377,0.553,70,76],[5.841,0.421,78,83],[6.274,0.168,84,87],[6.454,0.469,88,95],[6.935,0.204,96,99],[7.151,0.12,100,103],[7.284,0.457,104,108],[7.909,0.565,110,117],[8.486,0.24,118,121],[8.738,0.685,122,131],[10.337,0.144,133,137],[10.493,0.096,138,141],[10.601,0.312,142,146],[10.925,0.264,147,151],[11.202,0.132,152,155],[11.346,0.18,156,